*sarthi.txt*                                       Sarthi, a GUI for Neovim

Generated by `cargo xtask docs` from runtime/doc/sarthi.txt.in, the settings
in crates/rpc/src/sarthi/settings.rs and the Lua modules' annotations. Edit
those, not this file.

==============================================================================
CONTENTS                                                     *sarthi-contents*

    Introduction ....................................... |sarthi-intro|
    Settings ........................................... |sarthi-settings|
    Per-window settings ................................ |sarthi-w:sarthi|
    Lua module ......................................... |sarthi|
    Window functions ................................... |sarthi.api|

==============================================================================
INTRODUCTION                                                    *sarthi-intro*

Sarthi sets `vim.g.sarthi`, so a config or plugin shared with the TUI can
check it before using what only Sarthi has. Fonts are Neovim's own
'guifont' and 'linespace' options.

==============================================================================
SETTINGS                                                     *sarthi-settings*

Set with `require('sarthi').setup({ … })`, by section, e.g.
>lua
    require('sarthi').setup({
      shadow = { opacity = 0.5 },
      outline = { enabled = true, highlight = 'Comment' },
    })
<
Each section and key is optional: what isn't given keeps its value, at first
its default. setup() can be called again, e.g. from a keymap; it applies at
once. A mistake is an error at the call.

PER-WINDOW SETTINGS                                          *sarthi-w:sarthi*

The sections about a window (`scroll`, `shadow`, `outline`, `corners`,
`padding`) can be set for one window too, in its `w:sarthi` table: the same
sections with the same keys, but `exclude_filetypes`. Each key given replaces
the setting for that window; a window's `enabled` wins over the filetypes the
setting excludes.
>lua
    vim.w[win].sarthi = { outline = { enabled = true, width = 2 } }
<
|sarthi.api| sets it from the `sarthi` table of a window's config. A mistake
in a table set directly is shown once, and the window gets the settings until
it's fixed.

